  "status_banner": "PROMOTE \u2014 OK TO DOWNLOAD & SUBMIT (All Holdout, >1 km Far-Fault, Format & 65-Raster Uniqueness Gates Passed)",
  "hypothesis": "H68-AC3 (Local-Scarp + Footwall-Asymmetry + Fault-Tip-Relay Auto-Context Strand Refinement): Removing smooth basin-scale lookup bands (IR-68-BLOB-01) from Stage 1 in favor of 37 purely local topographic/geophysical/2m-LiDAR scarp & footwall-asymmetry channels, and iterating Tu (2008) auto-context twice (Stage 1 -> Stage 2 -> Stage 3) with +-1..15 px oriented probability offsets, anisotropic along/across-strike smooths (no sigma=10 px blob smooth), directional 1.5/3.0 km along-strike fault-tip relays, and damped rank-probability stacking will beat Stage 1 by > 2 SE (and 95% block-bootstrap CI > 0) on both all pixels and > 1 km far pixels while emitting crisp linear strands.",
  "mechanism": "Stage 1 predicts out-of-fold probabilities across 4 spatially blocked, 12-px-buffered quadrants using 37 local structural channels (elev_hp15, elev_asym, db_grad, db_hp15, elev_grad, elev_ridge_s2, 2m LiDAR lappos_max/relief/step_max/ex_max/scarp_contrast, and high-pass GeoDAWN ratios). Stages 2 and 3 train on 3 independent buffered component-hide draws (seeds 20, 21, 22; 11,321\u201311,572 withheld fault pixels per draw) where every catalogue-context feature is computed strictly from that draw's visible catalogue, then apply damped rank-probability sequential refinement (alpha2=0.22, alpha3=0.35) and 5x5 NMS emission outside a 2 px catalogue collar.",
  "named_non_fault_mimic_process": "Differential erosion along welded/non-welded Tertiary ash-flow tuff cooling-unit contacts, basaltic mesa caprock rims, and coalescing alluvial-fan bajada toes (which produce topographic slopes and radiometric contrasts but lack across-strike footwall/hangingwall elevation-gradient asymmetry, coincident depth-to-basement steps, and colinear along-strike probability continuity).",
